**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The pure shapes of an attachment and of copying a lab file in (001 §E 'References inside a kit are relative paths (forward slashes) plus the SHA-256 recorded at attach time', 'Attaching a file from outside the kit copies it into data/, keeping its name and suffixing on collision', 'A changed or missing data file is flagged on open and before each fit'; the S4.2 brief: `DataAttachment` is a `KitRelativePath` plus the `ContentHash` recorded at attach, and a file from outside is copied into `data/` or a chosen folder inside it, keeping its name, with ` (2)`, ` (3)`… on collision; .spec-md §5 `Kit` module). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs` (steps 122-131), after `KitDataFile` (step 123), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.2, every type following `AGENTS.md` (single-case unions carry `.value`, case names have two words, no `bool`). (1) `KitDataFolder of KitRelativePath`, a folder of the kit that lab files are copied into: `data` or a folder inside it (001 §A 'data/ … raw lab files (default home for attachments)'). `static member root : KitDataFolder` is `data`, the folder `initialiseKit` creates (step 125). `static member tryCreate (path : KitRelativePath) : Result<KitDataFolder, KitError>` keeps `data` and every path that starts `data/` (ordinal) and refuses any other with `InvalidKitPathErr` naming it. (2) `member this.copyTargetFor (leaf : FileName) (taken : KitRelativePath list) : Result<KitRelativePath, KitError>` on `KitDataFolder` is the one collision rule. It answers the first of `<folder>/<leaf>`, `<folder>/<stem> (2)<extension>`, `<folder>/<stem> (3)<extension>`, … that no path of `taken` equals ignoring case (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`, the Windows rule). The extension is the text from the leaf's last `.` when that `.` is not its first character, and empty otherwise: `run 1.csv` gives `run 1 (2).csv`, `archive.tar.gz` gives `archive.tar (2).gz`, `README` gives `README (2)` and `.hidden` gives `.hidden (2)`. Each candidate is made through `KitRelativePath.tryCreate` (step 123), so a leaf that cannot be a kit path answers its `InvalidKitPathErr`. `taken` is every file and folder directly in the folder, and the rule reads nothing. (3) `type KitFolder with member this.tryKitPathOf (file : FileName) : KitRelativePath option` answers the kit-relative path of an absolute file name that lies inside the folder, and `None` otherwise. Both texts have every `\` turned into `/`, and the folder's text loses a trailing `/`. When the file's text starts with the folder's text followed by `/`, ignoring case, the rest goes through `KitRelativePath.tryCreate`, whose `Ok` is the answer. Every other name is `None`, the folder itself and a sibling folder sharing a prefix (`C:/kits/a` against `C:/kits/ab/x.csv`) included. It touches no disk. (4) `LabFileSource = { file : FileName; content : FileByteContent }`, a lab file as the user picked it: its absolute name and its bytes. `FileByteContent` is `Softellect.Sys.Primitives.FileByteContent` (STL `Sys/Primitives.fs`), reused, not declared again (ELEV014). (5) `DataAttachment = { path : KitRelativePath; contentHash : ContentHash }`, the data file an experiment references: its path inside the kit and the SHA-256 recorded at attach (.spec-md §5). It never holds an absolute path. `type KitDataFile with member this.attachment : DataAttachment` answers the file's path and hash. (6) `DataAttachmentStatus` = `AttachedDataUnchanged` | `AttachedDataChanged of current : ContentHash` | `AttachedDataMissing`: unchanged, data changed since attach, or missing (001 §E). `member this.statusAgainst (currentOpt : KitDataFile option) : DataAttachmentStatus` on `DataAttachment` answers `AttachedDataMissing` for `None`, `AttachedDataUnchanged` for a file whose `contentHash` equals the recorded one, and `AttachedDataChanged` of the file's hash for any other. No other type, member, option or rule is added. Tests, new facts in `KitTests` (step 122). `a data folder is the kit's data folder or a folder inside it`: `KitDataFolder.root` is `data`; `tryCreate` keeps `data` and `data/raw/run 1`, and refuses `raw`, `library`, `datax` and `.oc/data` with `InvalidKitPathErr`. `a copy keeps its file name and takes the first free numbered suffix, ignoring case`: under `root`, `run 1.csv` with nothing taken answers `data/run 1.csv`; with `data/run 1.csv` taken, `data/run 1 (2).csv`; with that and `data/RUN 1 (2).CSV` taken, `data/run 1 (3).csv`. `archive.tar.gz`, `README` and `.hidden`, each taken once, answer `data/archive.tar (2).gz`, `data/README (2)` and `data/.hidden (2)`. Under `data/raw`, `a.csv` answers `data/raw/a.csv`, and a leaf `C:a.csv` answers `InvalidKitPathErr`. `a file is inside the kit when its absolute name lies under the kit folder`: over `KitFolder (FolderName "C:/kits/Optics")`, `C:/kits/Optics/data/run 1.csv`, `c:\KITS\optics\data\run 1.csv` and `C:/kits/Optics/notes.txt` answer `data/run 1.csv`, `data/run 1.csv` and `notes.txt`. `C:/kits/Optics`, `C:/kits/OpticsB/data/a.csv`, `D:/lab/a.csv` and `C:/kits/Optics/../a.csv` answer `None`. A folder text ending in `/` answers as the same folder. `an attachment records its data file's path and hash, and its status compares that hash with the file now`: a `KitDataFile` at `data/a.csv` with the hash of the UTF-8 bytes of `abc` (`ContentHash.ofBytes`, step 123) answers an attachment with that path and hash. That attachment against `Some` of the same file is `AttachedDataUnchanged`, against a file with the hash of `abd` is `AttachedDataChanged` of that hash, and against `None` is `AttachedDataMissing`.

**Acceptance.** After the attachment shapes land, `KitDataFolder.copyTargetFor` MUST keep a lab file's name and take the first free ` (n)` suffix ignoring case, `KitFolder.tryKitPathOf` MUST locate only names inside the kit folder, and `DataAttachment.statusAgainst` MUST answer unchanged, changed or missing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a data folder is the kit's data folder or a folder inside it`, `a copy keeps its file name and takes the first free numbered suffix, ignoring case`, `a file is inside the kit when its absolute name lies under the kit folder`, `an attachment records its data file's path and hash, and its status compares that hash with the file now`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.
